# BookHub project-specific Valgrind suppressions
#
# Usage — always combine with the system Qt suppression file:
#   valgrind \
#     --suppressions=/usr/share/doc/qt6-base-dev/valgrind.supp \
#     --suppressions=tools/valgrind.supp \
#     --leak-check=full \
#     --show-leak-kinds=definite \
#     --track-origins=yes \
#     QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen ./build/tests/test_library_service
#
# When to add entries here:
#   1. Run valgrind and spot a Memcheck:Leak in the "still reachable" or
#      "definitely lost" bucket that you've confirmed is a false positive.
#   2. Copy the call-stack frames from valgrind's output into a new entry.
#   3. Use wildcards (fun:* or obj:*) sparingly — be as specific as possible
#      to avoid accidentally suppressing real leaks.
#
# Entry format:
#   {
#      <descriptive-name>
#      Memcheck:<error-kind>
#      [match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible,reachable]
#      fun:<frame>    — exact function name
#      ...
#      obj:<pattern>  — shared library glob
#   }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite internal page cache
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite pre-allocates a page cache that is intentionally never freed for the
# lifetime of the process. This is "still reachable" by valgrind's definition
# but is not a leak.
{
   sqlite3_pcache_static
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:sqlite3PcacheOpen
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Qt SQLite plugin static initialisation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The QSQLITE driver is registered as a static plugin. Qt's plugin registry
# holds the factory forever (intentional singleton), which valgrind classifies
# as "still reachable".
{
   qsqlite_plugin_registry
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   obj:*libqsqlite*
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add project-specific suppressions below this line
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To generate a suppression entry automatically, run valgrind with:
#   --gen-suppressions=all
# and paste the generated block here, then give it a descriptive name.
